# LGR regression baseline: fork (builds/refined) vs upstream master (builds/release).
# Columns: <deck>  <fork==master tol>  <fork-serial==fork-parallel tol>
# Values: 1e-6..1e-1 = tightest matching relative tolerance; FAIL = no match;
#         "-" = a run did not complete (see status below), so no comparison.
#
# lgr_regression.sh exits non-zero if any cell here regresses (a passing
# tolerance gets looser or turns to FAIL). Tighten entries here as the fork's
# refinement is brought into agreement with master; run with -u to catch
# unexpected improvements that should be recorded.
#
# Current state (2026-06-14):
#   * Cartesian LGR (CARFIN, CARFIN1): bit-compatible with master and
#     parallel-consistent to 1e-6. These are the guard-rails.
#   * Corner-point (2D/3D) and FLEX: refinement diverges from master (FAIL);
#     mostly still parallel-self-consistent. Known gap in the fork's
#     corner-point refinement -- to be closed.
#   * CARFIN_GR (wells inside the LGR): diverges from master; parallel run
#     currently fails.
#   * 3DCORNERPOINT_XYZ-NON and CARFIN_FAULTS: do not run (the latter fails
#     in opm-common FAULTS parsing, unrelated to the grid).
#
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN                          1e-6  1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1                         1e-6  1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1-2DCORNERPOINT_XY        FAIL  1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1-3DCORNERPOINT_XYZ       FAIL  FAIL
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN1-3DCORNERPOINT_XYZ-NON   -     -
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN_FLEX                     FAIL  1e-6
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN_GR                       FAIL  -
SPE1CASE1_CARFIN_FAULTS                   -     -
